IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III.1 Reduction of Premiums for Employees Covered by a Provincial
-- Plan and for their Employers, Divisions 1 and 2: regs 76.01 to 76.08 (interpretation, adaptation, the standards of a
-- provincial plan, the premium reduction and its rate). Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial
-- plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified against the official text". No section GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATION. Where a province pays its own benefits for pregnancy and the care of new-born or adopted children
-- (QPIP is the instance the text itself names in reg 76.08), the employee's and the employer's premiums under Act
-- ss 67 and 68 are reduced by a published rate. The person is affected by the reduction; the standards for the plan
-- bind the province, the rate is the Commission's. Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a rate is a fraction (0.5% is 0.005).
-- Judgments the text leaves to others ("substantially the same persons", "substantially equivalent") are BOOLEAN
-- inputs named for the judgment and are never guessed (fork F15).

§ `Regulation 76.01 -- interpretation`

-- src:1177 | 76.01 The definitions in this section apply in this Part.
-- src:1178 | provincial benefits means allowances, money or other benefits, paid to a person under a provincial plan because of pregnancy or in respect of the care by that person of one or more of their new-born children or one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption. (prestations provinciales)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.01 "provincial benefits" (src:1177-1178)
GIVEN `the allowances, money or other benefits are paid to a person under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid because of pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more of their new-born children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.01 provincial benefits` IF
        `the allowances, money or other benefits are paid to a person under a provincial plan`
    AND (    `they are paid because of pregnancy`
          OR `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more of their new-born children`
          OR `they are paid in respect of the care by that person of one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption`)

-- "Agreement ... to establish a system for reducing employer's and employee's premiums where the payment of those
-- benefits would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act".
-- src:1179 | provincial plan means a plan, established under a provincial law, that provides for the payment of provincial benefits and in respect of which an agreement has been entered into between the Government of Canada and the province to establish a system for reducing employer’s and employee’s premiums where the payment of those benefits would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act. (régime provincial)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.01 "provincial plan" (src:1179)
GIVEN `the plan is established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement has been entered into between the Government of Canada and the province to establish a system for reducing employer's and employee's premiums where the payment of those benefits would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.01 provincial plan` IF
        `the plan is established under a provincial law`
    AND `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits`
    AND `an agreement has been entered into between the Government of Canada and the province to establish a system for reducing employer's and employee's premiums where the payment of those benefits would have the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act`

-- Only direct operating costs of providing benefits under ss 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 that fluctuate with the number of
-- claims processed count; "any fixed operating costs related to the administration of the Act" do not.
-- src:1180 | variable administrative costs means the amount of direct operating costs incurred to provide benefits under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 of the Act that fluctuate with the number of claims for such benefits that are processed, not including any fixed operating costs related to the administration of the Act. (frais administratifs variables)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.01 "variable administrative costs" (src:1180)
DECLARE `er4 Operating cost of the Act` HAS
    `er4 amount of the operating cost`                                                              IS A NUMBER
    `er4 direct cost of providing benefits under section 22, 23, 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `er4 cost fluctuates with the number of claims processed`                                       IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.01 "variable administrative costs" (src:1180)
GIVEN costs IS A LIST OF `er4 Operating cost of the Act`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.01 variable administrative costs` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `er4 amount of the operating cost`)
             (filter (GIVEN c YIELD     c's `er4 direct cost of providing benefits under section 22, 23, 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`
                                    AND c's `er4 cost fluctuates with the number of claims processed`)
                     costs))

§ `Regulation 76.02 -- adaptation of the Act and these Regulations`

-- The Part adapts the Act and the Regulations "as provided in this Part": the provisions it adapts are listed here,
-- each cited where the adaptation is encoded. A provision the Part does not mention is not adapted by it (NOTHING:
-- the text does not say that no other provision is adapted).
-- src:1183 | 76.02 For the purposes of this Part, the Act and these Regulations are adapted as provided in this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.02 (src:1183)
DECLARE `er4 Provision of the Act or the Regulations adapted for Part III.1` IS ONE OF
    `er4 the definition insured participant in section 58 of the Act`                      -- reg 76.11
    `er4 subsection 8(5) of the Act, weeks in receipt of benefits`                          -- reg 76.13
    `er4 subsection 10(13) of the Act, extension of the benefit period`                     -- reg 76.14
    `er4 subsection 10(12) of the Act, hospitalized child`                                   -- reg 76.15
    `er4 section 12 of the Act, the maximum number of weeks`                                 -- reg 76.19, 76.2
    `er4 paragraph 40(6)(b), the waiting period`                                             -- reg 76.22
    `er4 another provision`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.02 (src:1183)
GIVEN provision IS A `er4 Provision of the Act or the Regulations adapted for Part III.1`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 76.02 the Act and these Regulations are adapted for Part III.1 in respect of` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `er4 another provision` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Regulation 76.03 -- the standards of a provincial plan`

-- The plan must meet each of (a) to (f) "beginning on the day on which it takes effect". Two judgments are the
-- Commission's or the Minister's to make and so are inputs: that the plan covers "substantially the same persons" as
-- the insured persons (b), and that its global amount of benefits is "substantially equivalent to or greater than" the
-- federal (c) (fork F15).
-- src:1188 | 76.03 A provincial plan shall, beginning on the day on which it takes effect, meet the following requirements:
-- src:1189 | (a) the plan must provide for the payment of provincial benefits;
-- src:1190 | (b) the plan must, at a minimum, cover substantially the same persons as those who are insured persons under the Act;
-- src:1191 | (c) the global amount of provincial benefits payable to a person under the plan must be substantially equivalent to or greater than the global amount of benefits payable to a claimant under section 22 or 23 of the Act;
-- src:1192 | (d) the plan must provide that an applicant who has received at least one week of provincial benefits under it shall continue to receive such benefits for their full period of entitlement, even if, after receiving that first week of benefits, they become a resident of a different province;
-- src:1193 | (e) the plan must provide for premium adjustment payments to be made to the Receiver General by the province where the plan is established in respect of employer’s and employee’s premiums paid under the plan in respect of employees who are not covered by the plan because of their residency; and
-- src:1194 | (f) the plan must provide for the sharing, by the province with the Government of Canada, of information obtained in the course of administering the plan that is necessary for the administration of a premium reduction system established by this Part, as well as information prepared from that information.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.03 (src:1188-1194)
GIVEN `the day the plan takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the plan meets all of the requirements` IS A DATE
      `the plan provides for the payment of provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan covers, at a minimum, substantially the same persons as those who are insured persons under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the global amount of provincial benefits payable to a person is substantially equivalent to or greater than the global amount of benefits payable to a claimant under section 22 or 23 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan provides that an applicant who has received at least one week of provincial benefits continues to receive them for the full period of entitlement even after becoming a resident of a different province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan provides for premium adjustment payments to be made to the Receiver General by the province in respect of employer's and employee's premiums paid in respect of employees not covered because of their residency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan provides for the sharing by the province with the Government of Canada of information obtained in administering the plan that is necessary for the administration of a premium reduction system established by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.03 the provincial plan meets the requirements from the day it takes effect` IF
        `the day from which the plan meets all of the requirements` AT MOST `the day the plan takes effect`
    AND `the plan provides for the payment of provincial benefits`
    AND `the plan covers, at a minimum, substantially the same persons as those who are insured persons under the Act`
    AND `the global amount of provincial benefits payable to a person is substantially equivalent to or greater than the global amount of benefits payable to a claimant under section 22 or 23 of the Act`
    AND `the plan provides that an applicant who has received at least one week of provincial benefits continues to receive them for the full period of entitlement even after becoming a resident of a different province`
    AND `the plan provides for premium adjustment payments to be made to the Receiver General by the province in respect of employer's and employee's premiums paid in respect of employees not covered because of their residency`
    AND `the plan provides for the sharing by the province with the Government of Canada of information obtained in administering the plan that is necessary for the administration of a premium reduction system established by this Part`

§ `Regulation 76.04 to 76.08 -- the premium reduction`

-- src:1197 | 76.04 The employee’s and employer’s premiums payable under sections 67 and 68 of the Act, respectively, shall be reduced as provided by section 76.05 if the payment of provincial benefits to insured persons under a provincial plan would have the effect referred to in subsection 69(2) of the Act in respect of benefits payable to those persons under section 22 or 23 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.04 (src:1197)
GIVEN `the payment of provincial benefits to insured persons under a provincial plan would have the effect, in respect of benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act, of reducing or eliminating them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.04 the employee's and employer's premiums payable under sections 67 and 68 of the Act are to be reduced` IF
    `the payment of provincial benefits to insured persons under a provincial plan would have the effect, in respect of benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act, of reducing or eliminating them`

-- 76.05 reads "calculated by applying the premium reduction rate determined in accordance with section 76.06": the
-- reduction is the rate times the amount the premium rate itself is applied to (for the employee's premium, the
-- insurable earnings, Act s 67; out of range, piece ei3). How the rate applies to the employer's premium, which Act
-- s 68 makes 1.4 times the employees' premiums, is not worked out by the text: the caller supplies the base (fork F16).
-- src:1199 | 76.05 The premium reduction to be applied to employer’s and employee’s premiums shall be calculated by applying the premium reduction rate determined in accordance with section 76.06.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.05 (src:1199)
GIVEN `the amount to which the premium rate is applied` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium reduction rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.05 the premium reduction obtained by applying the premium reduction rate` MEANS
    `the amount to which the premium rate is applied` TIMES `the premium reduction rate`

§§ `Regulation 76.06 -- the premium reduction rate`

-- src:1200 | 76.06 (1) The premium reduction rate for a year is the rate determined by subtracting the rate determined under paragraph (b) from the rate determined under paragraph (a) and by rounding off the difference in accordance with section 66.4 of the Act:
-- src:1201 | (a) the rate determined by adding the following results, namely,
-- src:1202 | (i) the result obtained by dividing the estimated total amount of all benefits that will be paid under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 of the Act in respect of that year to all claimants who are not covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan established under a provincial law by the sum of the estimated total amount of insurable earnings in that year multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated amount of self-employed earnings in that year, taking into consideration the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year as calculated under section 4 of the Act, of self-employed persons who have entered into — or will enter into during that year — an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act, of all persons who are not covered by such a plan, and
-- src:1203 | (ii) the result obtained by dividing the estimated total amount of the variable administrative costs that will be incurred in that year to provide benefits under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 of the Act to all claimants who are not covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan established under a provincial law by the sum of the estimated total amount of insurable earnings in that year multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated amount of self-employed earnings in that year, taking into consideration the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year as calculated under section 4 of the Act, of self-employed persons who have entered into — or will enter into during that year — an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act, of all persons who are not covered by such a plan; and
-- src:1204 | (b) the rate determined by adding the following results, namely,
-- src:1205 | (i) the result obtained by dividing the estimated total amount of all benefits that will be paid under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 of the Act in respect of that year to all claimants who are covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan established under a provincial law by the sum of the estimated total amount of insurable earnings in that year multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated amount of self-employed earnings in that year, taking into consideration the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year as calculated under section 4 of the Act, of self-employed persons who have entered into — or will enter into during that year — an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act, of all persons who are covered by such a plan, and
-- src:1206 | (ii) the result obtained by dividing the estimated total amount of the variable administrative costs that will be incurred in that year to provide benefits under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 of the Act to all claimants who are covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan established under a provincial law by the sum of the estimated total amount of insurable earnings in that year multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated amount of self-employed earnings in that year, taking into consideration the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year as calculated under section 4 of the Act, of self-employed persons who have entered into — or will enter into during that year — an agreement under section 152.02 of the Act, of all persons who are covered by such a plan.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
DECLARE `er4 Estimates for one group of persons` HAS
    `er4 estimated total amount of all benefits paid under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 in respect of the year to claimants in the group`   IS A NUMBER   -- (a)(i), (b)(i)
    `er4 estimated total amount of the variable administrative costs incurred in the year to provide those benefits to claimants in the group`    IS A NUMBER   -- (a)(ii), (b)(ii)
    `er4 estimated total amount of insurable earnings in the year of the persons in the group`                                                   IS A NUMBER   -- the divisor, first term
    `er4 estimated amount of self-employed earnings in the year of the self-employed persons in the group who have entered or will enter into an agreement under section 152.02`   IS A NUMBER   -- the divisor, second term

-- The divisor in all four of (a)(i), (a)(ii), (b)(i), (b)(ii): "the sum of the estimated total amount of insurable
-- earnings in that year multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated amount of self-employed earnings in that year". The 2.4
-- is read as multiplying the insurable earnings alone, not the sum (fork F17).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
GIVEN group IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` MEANS
    (group's `er4 estimated total amount of insurable earnings in the year of the persons in the group` TIMES 2.4)
        PLUS group's `er4 estimated amount of self-employed earnings in the year of the self-employed persons in the group who have entered or will enter into an agreement under section 152.02`

-- A divisor that is not above zero gives no rate: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
GIVEN group IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.06(1)(a)(i) and (b)(i) the result obtained by dividing the estimated benefits by the divisor` MEANS
    IF `reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` group AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (group's `er4 estimated total amount of all benefits paid under sections 22, 23, 152.04 and 152.05 in respect of the year to claimants in the group`
                   DIVIDED BY `reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` group)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
GIVEN group IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.06(1)(a)(ii) and (b)(ii) the result obtained by dividing the estimated variable administrative costs by the divisor` MEANS
    IF `reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` group AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (group's `er4 estimated total amount of the variable administrative costs incurred in the year to provide those benefits to claimants in the group`
                   DIVIDED BY `reg 76.06(1) the sum of the estimated insurable earnings multiplied by 2.4 and the estimated self-employed earnings` group)

-- (a) is the rate for the claimants and persons NOT covered by a provincial plan, (b) the rate for those covered: each
-- is the sum of its (i) and (ii).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
GIVEN group IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.06(1)(a) and (b) the rate determined by adding the two results` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 76.06(1)(a)(i) and (b)(i) the result obtained by dividing the estimated benefits by the divisor` group
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST benefits THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 76.06(1)(a)(ii) and (b)(ii) the result obtained by dividing the estimated variable administrative costs by the divisor` group
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST costs THEN JUST (benefits PLUS costs)

-- "Rounding off the difference in accordance with section 66.4 of the Act" (out of range: Act s 66.4, piece ei3): to the
-- nearest one hundredth of one per cent, the higher when equidistant. Restated here as a local rule under this
-- regulation's own name, because ei3's rule cannot be imported (listed in NOTES.md, Cross-references).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.06(1) the rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent, as section 66.4 of the Act directs` MEANS
    (FLOOR ((rate TIMES 10000) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 10000

-- The premium reduction rate for a year: (a), the rate for those NOT covered, minus (b), the rate for those covered,
-- rounded; determined only on actuarial estimates (2) and having regard to the factors of section 66 of the Act (3).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(1) (src:1200-1206)
GIVEN `the persons not covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan` IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
      `the persons covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan` IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.06(1) the premium reduction rate for a year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 76.06(1)(a) and (b) the rate determined by adding the two results` `the persons not covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST notCovered THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 76.06(1)(a) and (b) the rate determined by adding the two results` `the persons covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST covered THEN
            JUST (`reg 76.06(1) the rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent, as section 66.4 of the Act directs` (notCovered MINUS covered))

-- src:1207 | (2) Actuarial estimates shall be used to determine the estimated amounts referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(2) (src:1207)
GIVEN `the estimated amounts are actuarial estimates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.06(2) actuarial estimates are used to determine the estimated amounts` IF
    `the estimated amounts are actuarial estimates`

-- src:1208 | (3) The results referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) shall be determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06(3) (src:1208)
GIVEN `the results have been determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.06(3) the results are determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act` IF
    `the results have been determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act`

-- The whole of regulation 76.06: a rate only if (2) and (3) are met as well.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.06 (src:1200-1208)
GIVEN `the estimated amounts are actuarial estimates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results have been determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons not covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan` IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
      `the persons covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan` IS A `er4 Estimates for one group of persons`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.06 the premium reduction rate determined as the regulation requires` MEANS
    IF     `reg 76.06(2) actuarial estimates are used to determine the estimated amounts` `the estimated amounts are actuarial estimates`
       AND `reg 76.06(3) the results are determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act` `the results have been determined having regard to the same factors as those set out in section 66 of the Act`
    THEN `reg 76.06(1) the premium reduction rate for a year` `the persons not covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan` `the persons covered by a provincial plan or any other similar plan`
    ELSE NOTHING
